          {
            "x": 2.178649237472767,
            "y": 12.910611231371064,
            "width": 92.73743016759778,
            "height": 86.09271523178808,
            "action": {
              "library": "H5P.AdvancedText 1.1",
              "params": {
                "text": "<p><strong>Friendship with Brahms</strong><br />\nJohannes Brahms became a close friend of the family, and after Robert's death, he and Clara maintained a close, albeit platonic, relationship. Brahms was deeply inspired by Clara's musicality and dedication.</p>\n\n<p><strong>Later Years</strong><br />\nIn her later years, Clara's renown as a pianist overshadowed her composing. However, she continued to be a respected figure in the music community, teaching at the Hoch Conservatory in Frankfurt.</p>\n\n<p><strong>Legacy and Memory</strong><br />\nClara Schumann passed away in 1896, but her influence as a pianist, teacher, and composer endures. She is remembered as one of the most important musicians of the Romantic era, and her compositions, once neglected, have gained recognition in recent times.</p>\n"
              },
              "metadata": {
                "contentType": "Text",
                "license": "U",
                "title": "Unbenannt: Text",
                "defaultLanguage": "en"
              },
